---
import { DollarSign } from '@lucide/astro';
import EmailCta from '../EmailCta.astro';
import PageShareButton from '../PageShareButton.astro';
import PeerSharePrompt from '../PeerSharePrompt.astro';
import SectionLastUpdated from '../SectionLastUpdated.astro';
import { roleEmailCtas, visitorModes } from '../../lib/email-drafts.mts';

const visionSignals = [
  {
    title: 'What I Sell Now',
    points: [
      'One offer: Backend Reliability Sprint (5-10 business days).',
      'Input: one live backend bottleneck. Output: shipped fix, tests, and handoff notes.',
      'Best buyer: founder/CTO of an API-heavy product team blocked on delivery.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'How It Evolves',
    points: [
      'Every sprint produces reusable checklists, templates, and implementation patterns.',
      'Repeated patterns are packaged into productized reliability modules.',
      'Goal: move from one-off delivery to repeatable service revenue with better margins.',
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Operating Constraint',
    points: [
      'This is currently a solo build with no external funding and no team.',
      'Execution happens alongside a full-time job, so pilot slots stay limited by design.',
      'Funding is an accelerator, not a prerequisite for starting paid work.',
    ],
  },
];
---

<section aria-labelledby="vision-heading" class="mode-hero">
  <div class="headline-row">
    <span aria-hidden="true" class="headline-icon"
      ><DollarSign size={86} /></span
    >
    <h1 id="vision-heading">
      Service-first: Backend Reliability Sprints for API-heavy teams.
    </h1>
  </div>
  <div class="cta-row">
    {
      roleEmailCtas.vision.map((cta) => (
        <EmailCta cta={cta} mode={visitorModes.vision} />
      ))
    }
    <a
      class="cta-secondary"
      data-cta="Open Website System"
      data-cta-mode={visitorModes.vision}
      href="/operating-system"
    >
      Open Website System
    </a>
    <PageShareButton
      label="Share with investor"
      shareRole="Investor / Advisor"
      shareText="Sharing this execution-focused profile for investor review."
      shareTitle="Robertas Rudys | Investor / Advisor"
      source="vision_hero_cta"
    />
  </div>
  <noscript>
    <p class="cta-note">
      Email links require JavaScript. Please enable JavaScript to contact me.
    </p>
  </noscript>
  <p class="cta-note">
    Current stage: pre-funding, solo, limited pilot capacity. Request investment
    details for roadmap and milestone gates.
  </p>
</section>

<PeerSharePrompt
  message="Forward this profile to one investor or advisor reviewing execution-focused builders."
/>

<section aria-labelledby="vision-summary" class="card">
  <h2 id="vision-summary">Overview</h2>
  <SectionLastUpdated />
  <p>
    The business starts as paid, fixed-scope execution. I take one concrete
    backend bottleneck, ship a production-safe fix, and document what was done
    so teams can keep moving. The long-term plan is to productize repeated
    reliability work into reusable modules and playbooks.
  </p>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="vision-learn" class="card">
  <h2 id="vision-learn">What You Will Learn Here</h2>
  <SectionLastUpdated />
  <ul>
    <li>How service-first execution can evolve into productized offerings</li>
    <li>How to evaluate pre-scale opportunities with milestone-gated logic</li>
    <li>How to separate execution signal from traction storytelling</li>
    <li>How constraints should shape capital allocation decisions</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="vision-products" class="card">
  <h2 id="vision-products">What This Is</h2>
  <SectionLastUpdated />
  <ul>
    <li>Today: a productized service called Backend Reliability Sprint.</li>
    <li>
      Delivery model: one bottleneck, one fixed-scope sprint, clear acceptance
      criteria, and handoff-ready output.
    </li>
    <li>
      Revenue model now: paid sprint blocks and selective repeat engagements.
    </li>
    <li>
      Productization path next: turn repeated fixes into reusable reliability
      modules, templates, and onboarding workflows.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Commercial terms (current)</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Capacity: up to 2 pilot sprints per month</li>
    <li>Start window: first available slot in 2-4 weeks</li>
    <li>
      Required inputs: repository access, production context, and one named
      owner for acceptance sign-off
    </li>
    <li>
      Pricing model: fixed-scope sprint pricing agreed before kickoff, no open
      ended time-and-materials scope
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="vision-signals" class="card">
  <h2 id="vision-signals">Strategic Signals</h2>
  {
    visionSignals.map((signal) => (
      <article>
        <h3>{signal.title}</h3>
        <ul>
          {signal.points.map((point) => (
            <li>{point}</li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </article>
    ))
  }
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="vision-trajectory" class="card">
  <h2 id="vision-trajectory">Timeline and Plan</h2>
  <p>
    Plan under current constraints: keep scope narrow, close paid pilots, and
    compound each engagement into reusable assets. No fake scale assumptions.
  </p>
  <h3>Phase roadmap</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Phase 1 (0-3 months): close a small number of paid sprints and publish
      measurable before/after case studies.
    </li>
    <li>
      Phase 2 (3-9 months): standardize recurring fixes into reusable delivery
      modules and improve time-to-ship per sprint.
    </li>
    <li>
      Phase 3 (9-18 months): run a productized reliability line with repeatable
      onboarding, stable scope, and predictable monthly throughput.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Signals tracked now</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Pilot-to-repeat conversion rate by cohort</li>
    <li>Median time from signed scope to production release</li>
    <li>Repeat revenue share and gross margin stability</li>
    <li>Referral-driven pipeline share from delivered projects</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Baseline and target discipline</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Current stage baseline: pre-funding and pre-scale (metrics published as
      pilots close)
    </li>
    <li>
      Phase 1 target: close paid pilots and publish measurable before/after
      outcomes
    </li>
    <li>Phase 2 target: demonstrate repeat demand and improved time-to-ship</li>
    <li>
      Phase 3 target: show predictable monthly throughput with stable scope and
      margin
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h3>What funding changes</h3>
  <p>
    Funding increases capacity and speed: more sprint volume, faster
    productization, and earlier go-to-market for reusable modules. It does not
    change the core model.
  </p>
  <p>
    Any funding remains milestone-gated and tied to shipped outcomes, repeat
    demand, and revenue quality thresholds.
  </p>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="vision-gates" class="card">
  <h2 id="vision-gates">Milestone Gates (Falsifiable)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Gate 1: close at least 3 paid pilot sprints with documented baseline,
      shipped output, and post-release check.
    </li>
    <li>
      Gate 2: convert at least 1 pilot into repeat paid work under a second
      scoped engagement.
    </li>
    <li>
      Gate 3: publish a repeatable delivery playbook that reduces onboarding and
      execution variance across engagements.
    </li>
    <li>
      If gates fail: keep scope narrow, avoid scale hiring, and rework offer
      design before capital expansion.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Investor Decision Rule</h3>
  <p>
    Treat this as an execution thesis, not a traction story. Funding case is
    invalid until paid pilot data shows repeat demand and delivery quality under
    real constraints.
  </p>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="vision-diligence" class="card">
  <h2 id="vision-diligence">Investor Diligence Snapshot</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Available now: operating model, commercial terms, scope constraints, and
      milestone logic.
    </li>
    <li>
      Not available yet: audited traction history, stable cohort data, and
      mature unit economics.
    </li>
    <li>
      Evidence publication rule: publish measurable pilot data only after enough
      sample depth to avoid misleading conclusions.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Observable Facts On This Page</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Current operating mode is declared: solo, pre-funding, limited capacity
    </li>
    <li>
      Commercial constraints are explicit: up to 2 pilot sprints/month, 2-4 week
      start window
    </li>
    <li>
      Milestone gates include explicit fail-path behavior if targets are missed
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Current Hard Limits</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>No audited revenue history published on-page</li>
    <li>No cohort retention curve or repeat-purchase trend published</li>
    <li>No validated moat evidence beyond operator execution quality claims</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="vision-capital" class="card">
  <h2 id="vision-capital">Capital Use Logic (If Raised)</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      First priority: increase delivery throughput without degrading quality
      gates.
    </li>
    <li>
      Second priority: turn repeated sprint patterns into reusable modules and
      onboarding assets.
    </li>
    <li>
      Third priority: measured go-to-market experiments tied to repeat demand
      signals, not top-line vanity metrics.
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="vision-conversation" class="card">
  <h2 id="vision-conversation">Best Fit For Investor Conversation</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Investors evaluating service-first models with a clear productization path
    </li>
    <li>
      Advisors who can pressure-test milestone gates and capital allocation
    </li>
    <li>
      Operators able to validate unit economics and repeat-revenue assumptions
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>
